NAME
       engine - RTT-Inside computational core for resonance-time operations

SYNOPSIS
       The Engine is invoked indirectly through WRSADC and the 3-Pack cycle.
       It is not executed directly from the shell.

DESCRIPTION
       The RTT-Inside Engine is the inner computational core of the
       TriadicFrameworks system. It performs resonance-time calculations,
       coherence modeling, structural propagation, and operator execution.

       The Engine does not interact with the outside world directly. All
       external calls must pass through WRSADC, which provides boundary
       safety, structural-awareness metadata, and triadic wrapping.

       The Engine is responsible for:
           • resonance-time computation
           • coherence and alignment modeling
           • operator execution
           • structural propagation
           • state evolution within RTT-Inside space

       The Engine is pure logic. It assumes all inputs have already been
       validated, aligned, and triad-structured by WRSADC.

ARCHITECTURE
       The Engine operates on three conceptual layers:

       1. Resonance Layer
              Computes resonance-time relationships, coherence fields,
              and structural harmonics.

       2. Operator Layer
              Executes domain-specific operators, transformations, and
              RTT-native functions.

       3. Propagation Layer
              Updates internal state, lineage, and structural maps based
              on operator results.

       These layers are not exposed directly. They are orchestrated by
       WRSADC and structured by the 3-Pack.

WORKFLOW
       1. User invokes an action (shell or Python).
       2. WRSADC performs boundary checks and structural-awareness injection.
       3. WRSADC wraps the action in a triadic cycle (P1 → P2 → P3).
       4. The Engine receives a safe, aligned operation.
       5. The Engine computes resonance-time effects and operator results.
       6. WRSADC returns the result and updates lineage.

       The Engine never receives raw or unstructured input.

INTERFACE
       The Engine is accessed through WRSADCCore:

              from wrsadc_core import WRSADCCore
              core = WRSADCCore()
              core.dispatch(fn)

       The Engine does not expose public methods. All calls must be
       mediated by WRSADC.

RESPONSIBILITIES
       • Execute RTT-native operators.
       • Maintain internal resonance-time state.
       • Propagate structural-awareness metadata.
       • Ensure coherence across triadic cycles.
       • Produce deterministic, reproducible results.

NON-RESPONSIBILITIES
       • Boundary safety (handled by WRSADC).
       • Logging or state files (handled by 3PAK Shell).
       • User interaction (handled externally).
       • Primitive sequencing (handled by the 3-Pack).

WHEN TO USE THE ENGINE
       The Engine is used implicitly whenever:
           • a WRSADC dispatch occurs
           • a triadic cycle wraps an operation
           • RTT-native computation is required
           • structural propagation must occur

       The Engine should not be invoked directly.

FILES
       wrsadc_core.py
              Dispatch interface to the Engine.

       wrsadc_shell.sh
              Boundary layer for shell-level operations.

       3pak-shell/
              Provides triadic primitives and environment setup.

NOTES
       The Engine is the innermost component of the TriadicFrameworks stack.
       It is protected by WRSADC and structured by the 3-Pack. All higher-
       order patterns ultimately resolve into Engine operations.

